> parse [1, 2, 3][i]
[1, 2, 3][i]
> parse [1, 2.5, x][i]
[1, 2.5, real(x)][i]
> parse [[1, 2], [3, 4]][i]
[[1, 2], [3, 4]][i]
> parse [[1, 2], [3, 4]][1][0]
3
> parse [[1, 2], [3, 4]][1][j]
[3, 4][j]
> parse [x+1, x*2][i]
[(x + 1), (2 * x)][i]
> parse [1][0]
1
> parse [1, 2, 3][i+1]
[1, 2, 3][(i + 1)]
> parse [sin x, cos x][i]
[sin(real(x)), cos(real(x))][i]
> T = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
> parse T[1]
[3, 4]
> parse T[1][0]
3
> parse T[1][j]
[3, 4][j]
> f(i) = [10, 20, 30][i] where i in 0..2
  note: i has no type: inferred int from the integer operations in the body
> show f
f(i: int) = [10, 20, 30][i]  where i >= 0 && i <= 2
  -> int
> range f
range of f -> int:
  10..30
  fits in u5
  over all 3 points of the domain
